From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Sun, 2 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: make effect and card iteration order independent of
 addresses

Stock ygopro-core keeps several containers keyed by pointer and then walks
them in a way that sends messages, calls Lua or changes game state. The walk
order is the hash or address order, so two binaries with the same source
meaning (a different field size, a different allocator state) can play the
same duel differently. The 200 seed differential run found 6 seeds where two
hand cards lose a client hint (MSG_CARD_HINT / MSG_PLAYER_HINT, hint 7) in a
different order.

Registered effects get a unique initial_id once, in card::add_effect or
field::add_effect, and it never changes afterwards. Cards get a unique
cardid in interpreter::register_card. These ids are the new order key. A card enters unique_cards and
the grant maps only when it is on the field, so its cardid is final then.

Changed containers and why the order was observable:
- effects.pheff, effects.cheff (unordered_set): field::reset_phase and
  field::reset_chain call remove_effect, which sends the hint messages.
  processor.cpp also builds select_chains from pheff (EFFECT_SET_CONTROL).
- effects.spsummon_count_eff (unordered_set): effect::is_available runs the
  Lua condition and can assign effect::id, so the walk order changes Lua
  calls and later effect order.
- effects.oath (unordered_map): field::remove_oath_effect removes effects in
  walk order, which sends hint messages.
- effects.grant_effect gain_effects (unordered_map<card*, effect*>):
  field::erase_grant_effect removes the granted effects in walk order.
- card::indexer and field_effect::indexer, type effect_indexer
  (unordered_map): card::reset, card::replace_effect and the hand shuffle
  hint loop in field::shuffle send hint messages in walk order.
- core.quick_f_chain, type instant_f_list (map with the default pointer
  compare): the QuickEffect step builds select_chains from it.
- core.delayed_quick, core.delayed_quick_tmp (set of pair<effect*, tevent>,
  pointer compare): the QuickEffect step builds select_chains and chain ids
  from it. The new compare uses the effect initial_id, then the event
  content (ids, codes, cardids, group content). It keeps the stock
  tevent::operator< as the last tie break, so two events that are equal in
  content stay distinct, as before.
- core.unique_cards (unordered_set<card*>): check_unique_onfield returns the
  unique_effect of the first match, and adjust_self_destroy_set calls
  get_unique_target. It is now a card_set (cardid order).

Comparator: effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr orders by initial_id and uses the
address only as a tie break. Verified for every insert site that initial_id is
final and unique before the effect enters a container: card::add_effect sets
it before any insert; field::add_effect sets it when the effect has no
handler, and an effect with a handler already went through card::add_effect.
clone() copies initial_id, but a clone has no handler, so it gets a new id at
registration. Lookups of an unregistered effect (card::add_effect starts with
indexer.find) need the address tie break, or a clone would match its source.
Plain effect_sort_by_initial_id would be wrong there, so it is not used.
No unregistered effect is ever inserted in a keyed container.

Freed effects: the new compares read the effects in a container, and stock
compared only addresses. The re-keyed field containers remove an effect
before it goes into core.reseted_effects. The processor containers
quick_f_chain, delayed_quick and delayed_quick_tmp are cleared at Turn step
20 and at every phase start, and PointEvent step 10 clears delayed_quick. In
turn 1 they can still hold entries from the Startup events when Turn step 0
frees core.reseted_effects, and Turn step 1 can insert more entries before
the first clear in step 2. Turn step 0 now drops each entry whose effect or
event reason_effect is in core.reseted_effects, before the delete loop. No
PointEvent reads these containers between Startup and Turn step 2, and in
stock any read of such an entry was a use after free, so no defined
behaviour changes.

Sites checked and left unchanged:
- effects.rechargeable: effect::recharge only sets count_limit.
- core.reseted_effects (set<effect*>) and duel::uncopy: may hold
  unregistered effects. The walk only calls duel::delete_effect, which
  clears pointers and releases Lua registry references. It sends no message
  and calls no Lua code. Only the heap layout depends on the order.
- core.readjust_map, card::relations, card::relate_effect: lookup, insert
  or erase only. card::reset erases relations without a side effect.
- duel::cards, groups, effects, assumes: the destructor, duel::clear,
  delete_effect (clears pointers), restore_assumes (clears maps) and
  Duel.GetCardFromCardID (unique id) do not depend on the order.
- effects.disable_check_set, card_set and group::container: ordered by
  cardid (card_sort does not compare pointers).
- grant_effect.sorted: already ordered by initial_id upstream.
- card::reset_effect_count, card::filter_disable_related_cards,
  card::get_own_effects: they only recharge, fill an ordered set, or sort by
  effect::id.
- std::sort with effect_sort_id and card::card_operation_sort compare ids,
  locations and sequences, not addresses. effect::id is unique because every
  assignment uses infos.field_id++.
- Integer keyed unordered_maps (effect_count_map, spsummon_once_map,
  action_counter_t, attacker_map, coroutine_map, data_cache): the hash of an
  integer does not depend on an address.
- processor SortChain sort_map (map keyed by chain address): it is only
  looked up, never walked.
- Lua pairs() over tables keyed by userdata hashes by address. That is in the
  card scripts and in Lua, not in the core. The differential test removes it
  with LUA_FIXED_SEED.
---
 containers_fwd.h | 11 +++++++++--
 effect.cpp       |  6 ++++++
 field.cpp        | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 field.h          | 23 +++++++++++++++--------
 processor.cpp    | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 81 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/containers_fwd.h b/containers_fwd.h
index 32fc094..17057d6 100644
--- a/containers_fwd.h
+++ b/containers_fwd.h
@@ -25,7 +25,6 @@ using card_set = std::set<card*, card_sort>;
 class effect;
 using effect_vector = std::vector<effect*>;
 using effect_container = std::multimap<uint32_t, effect*>;
-using effect_indexer = std::unordered_map<effect*, effect_container::iterator>;
 using effect_set = std::vector<effect*>;
 using effect_set_v = effect_set;
 
@@ -36,12 +35,20 @@ struct effect_sort_by_id {
 struct effect_sort_by_initial_id {
 	bool operator()(effect* e1, effect* e2) const;
 };
+// Orders by registration (initial_id), and by address only when two effects have the same initial_id.
+// Registered effects have unique initial_ids, so their order never depends on an address.
+// The tie break makes a lookup of an unregistered effect (a clone keeps the initial_id of its source,
+// a new effect has 0) safe: it never matches another effect.
+struct effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr {
+	bool operator()(const effect* e1, const effect* e2) const;
+};
+using effect_indexer = std::map<effect*, effect_container::iterator, effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr>;
 
 struct chain;
 using chain_array = std::vector<chain>;
 using chain_list = std::list<chain>;
 
-using instant_f_list = std::map<effect*, chain>;
+using instant_f_list = std::map<effect*, chain, effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr>;
 
 struct tevent;
 using event_list = std::list<tevent>;
diff --git a/effect.cpp b/effect.cpp
index 7b316c3..5f72b83 100644
--- a/effect.cpp
+++ b/effect.cpp
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
  *
  * SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later
  */
+#include <functional> //std::less
 #include <vector>
 #include "card.h"
 #include "duel.h"
@@ -20,6 +21,11 @@ bool effect_sort_by_id::operator()(effect* e1, effect* e2) const {
 bool effect_sort_by_initial_id::operator()(effect* e1, effect* e2) const {
 	return e1->initial_id < e2->initial_id;
 }
+bool effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr::operator()(const effect* e1, const effect* e2) const {
+	if(e1->initial_id != e2->initial_id)
+		return e1->initial_id < e2->initial_id;
+	return std::less<const effect*>()(e1, e2);
+}
 int32_t effect::is_disable_related() {
 	if (code == EFFECT_IMMUNE_EFFECT || code == EFFECT_DISABLE || code == EFFECT_CANNOT_DISABLE || code == EFFECT_FORBIDDEN)
 		return TRUE;
diff --git a/field.cpp b/field.cpp
index f0c4c66..5cf6590 100644
--- a/field.cpp
+++ b/field.cpp
@@ -64,6 +64,39 @@ bool tevent::operator< (const tevent& rhs) const {
 				 rhs.event_code, rhs.event_value, rhs.reason,
 				 rhs.event_player, rhs.reason_player, rhs.global_id);
 }
+// Two delayed events with the same effect and the same content keep the order of the stock comparator
+// (tevent::operator<, which compares addresses). Everything before that is address free.
+bool processor::delayed_effect_sort::operator()(const std::pair<effect*, tevent>& lhs, const std::pair<effect*, tevent>& rhs) const {
+	if(lhs.first != rhs.first)
+		return effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr()(lhs.first, rhs.first);
+	const tevent& a = lhs.second;
+	const tevent& b = rhs.second;
+	const auto ka = std::tie(a.global_id, a.event_code, a.event_value, a.reason, a.event_player, a.reason_player);
+	const auto kb = std::tie(b.global_id, b.event_code, b.event_value, b.reason, b.event_player, b.reason_player);
+	if(ka != kb)
+		return ka < kb;
+	const uint32_t ta = a.trigger_card ? a.trigger_card->cardid : 0;
+	const uint32_t tb = b.trigger_card ? b.trigger_card->cardid : 0;
+	if(ta != tb)
+		return ta < tb;
+	const uint32_t ra = a.reason_effect ? a.reason_effect->initial_id : 0;
+	const uint32_t rb = b.reason_effect ? b.reason_effect->initial_id : 0;
+	if(ra != rb)
+		return ra < rb;
+	group* ga = a.event_cards;
+	group* gb = b.event_cards;
+	if((ga != nullptr) != (gb != nullptr))
+		return gb != nullptr;
+	if(ga && gb && ga != gb) {
+		const auto& ca = ga->container;
+		const auto& cb = gb->container;
+		if(std::lexicographical_compare(ca.begin(), ca.end(), cb.begin(), cb.end(), card_sort()))
+			return true;
+		if(std::lexicographical_compare(cb.begin(), cb.end(), ca.begin(), ca.end(), card_sort()))
+			return false;
+	}
+	return a < b;
+}
 field::field(duel* _pduel, const OCG_DuelOptions& options) :pduel(_pduel), player({ {options.team1, options.team2} }) {
 	core.duel_options = options.flags;
 	nil_event.event_code = 0;
diff --git a/field.h b/field.h
index 3a573c2..8151a2f 100644
--- a/field.h
+++ b/field.h
@@ -114,9 +114,12 @@ struct player_info {
 	}
 };
 struct field_effect {
-	using oath_effects = std::unordered_map<effect*, effect*>;
-	using effect_collection = std::unordered_set<effect*>;
-	using gain_effects = std::unordered_map<card*, effect*>;
+	// Every container below that is walked in a way that sends messages, calls Lua or changes the game
+	// state is ordered by registration (or card id), never by address. See patches/README.md.
+	using oath_effects = std::map<effect*, effect*, effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr>;
+	using effect_collection = std::unordered_set<effect*>; // only for rechargeable: recharge() has no side effect
+	using sorted_effect_collection = std::set<effect*, effect_sort_by_initial_id_ptr>;
+	using gain_effects = std::map<card*, effect*, card_sort>;
 	struct grant_effect_container {
 		std::unordered_map<effect*, gain_effects> unsorted;
 		std::map<effect*, gain_effects*, effect_sort_by_initial_id> sorted;
@@ -150,10 +153,10 @@ struct field_effect {
 	effect_container continuous_effect;
 	effect_indexer indexer;
 	oath_effects oath;
-	effect_collection pheff;
-	effect_collection cheff;
+	sorted_effect_collection pheff;
+	sorted_effect_collection cheff;
 	effect_collection rechargeable;
-	effect_collection spsummon_count_eff;
+	sorted_effect_collection spsummon_count_eff;
 
 	card_set disable_check_set;
 
@@ -197,7 +200,11 @@ using return_card_code = return_card_generic<std::pair<uint32_t, uint32_t>>;
 struct processor {
 	using option_vector = std::vector<uint64_t>;
 	using processor_list = std::list<processor_unit>;
-	using delayed_effect_collection = std::set<std::pair<effect*, tevent>>;
+	// Ordered by effect registration and event content, never by address (see delayed_effect_sort in field.cpp).
+	struct delayed_effect_sort {
+		bool operator()(const std::pair<effect*, tevent>& lhs, const std::pair<effect*, tevent>& rhs) const;
+	};
+	using delayed_effect_collection = std::set<std::pair<effect*, tevent>, delayed_effect_sort>;
 	using effect_count_map = std::unordered_map<uint64_t, uint32_t>;
 	struct chain_limit_t {
 		chain_limit_t(int32_t f, int32_t p): function(f), player(p) {}
@@ -284,7 +291,7 @@ struct processor {
 	effect_set_v extra_szone_effects;
 	std::set<effect*> reseted_effects;
 	std::unordered_map<card*, uint32_t> readjust_map;
-	std::unordered_set<card*> unique_cards[2];
+	card_set unique_cards[2];
 	effect_count_map effect_count_code;
 	effect_count_map effect_count_code_duel;
 	effect_count_map effect_count_code_chain;
diff --git a/processor.cpp b/processor.cpp
index d2c6c09..d654000 100644
--- a/processor.cpp
+++ b/processor.cpp
@@ -3260,6 +3260,24 @@ bool field::process(Processors::Turn& arg) {
 	case 0: {
 		//Pre Draw
 		core.used_event.clear();
+		// These containers compare by effect ids, so an insert or erase reads the effects in
+		// them. In turn 1 they can still hold entries from the Startup events (the first clear
+		// is in step 2). Drop the entries that point to an effect freed below.
+		auto freed = [&](effect* peffect) { return peffect && core.reseted_effects.count(peffect); };
+		for(auto it = core.quick_f_chain.begin(); it != core.quick_f_chain.end();) {
+			if(freed(it->first) || freed(it->second.evt.reason_effect))
+				it = core.quick_f_chain.erase(it);
+			else
+				++it;
+		}
+		for(auto* delayed : { &core.delayed_quick, &core.delayed_quick_tmp }) {
+			for(auto it = delayed->begin(); it != delayed->end();) {
+				if(freed(it->first) || freed(it->second.reason_effect))
+					it = delayed->erase(it);
+				else
+					++it;
+			}
+		}
 		for(auto& peffect : core.reseted_effects) {
 			pduel->delete_effect(peffect);
 		}
